hi this is presh talker in this video  i'm going to describe how an nfl team  with no wins could actually make the  playoffs  for now this remains a theoretical  possibility  the team with the worst record to have  made the playoffs is the seattle  seahawks at seven and nine  but who knows what will happen this year  or in the future  in this video we're going to do a  mathematical calculation  we're going to look at the lowest number  of wins you can have and still make the  playoffs  we're going to show the answer is zero  the other topic is we're going to see  the most number of losses a team could  have and still make the playoffs and  that answer is 13 losses  let's look at how the nfl structures its  game and schedules  there are two two conferences the afc  and the nfc  and within each conference are four  divisions  and each of these divisions  represents four teams and each division  is guaranteed a playoff spot  each team plays 16 games in a year  four of these games are against another  division within the same conference  there are another four games  that are scheduled to a division in  another conference  there are also two games that are played  within the same conference but in  different divisions  and finally the most important part is  there are six games played within the  same division  so each of the four teams within the  division play each other twice  now let's calculate the least number of  wins a team in a division could have and  still make the playoffs  so we're going to try and make all four  of the teams in the division really bad  so we're going to say those teams lose  all four of their games in the same  conference  playing the other division  they can also all lose all four games  against the other conference and they  could also lose two games against the  other divisional rivals in the same  conference where it gets tricky is where  they play the same division  since we don't want anyone to have wins  we could say all of those games end up  in ties  this would leave a team with a record of  0 10 and 6 and all four teams could  actually have this  meaning they would have no wins and one  of them would make the playoffs  what if we want to know the most number  of losses  well once again we can say that each of  the four teams is going to lose  against  the divisions they play against within  the same conference and the other  conference  they can also lose the remaining  divisional games in the same conference  now in terms of the same division the  most losses you could have is three  and there's a mathematical reason for  this  the reason is that every loss for one  team will be a win for another  because of the way the head-to-head  matchups are set up  so mathematically this means the best  team within the division  won't have more than three losses  and this is by the pigeonhole principle  so the worst team in a division  the best team could have a record of 3  and 13 all four of them could have that  and still make the playoffs it's really  weird that a zero win team or three win  team could actually make the playoffs  but that's how the nfl playoff system is  currently formatted  it's no wonder people are calling for  changes in the system please subscribe  to my channel you can support me on  patreon  catch me on my blog mind your decisions  on twitter at preshtalwalker  and you can get my books listed on my  website
 

